"body": "Softmax turns raw scores into a probability distribution that sums to 1. For each class, it divides the exponential of the score by the sum of all exponentials.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nIn the chart, each bar shows the resulting probability for a class from two independent predictions. Prediction A favors the middle class (Dog) slightly more than Prediction B, while Prediction B gives the highest weight to Dog.\n\nThe difference between the two sets of probabilities quantifies how the models disagree: the larger the gap, the stronger the disagreement for that class.\n\nBecause probabilities always sum to 1, a higher value for one class forces lower values for the others, making the comparison directly interpretable.\n",
