  "body": "Softmax maps raw model scores into a probability distribution over multiple classes. Given logit vector $z$, the probability for class $i$ is $\\sigma(z)_i = \\frac{e^{z_i}}{\\sum_{j} e^{z_j}}$.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nComparing two prediction vectors requires looking at how probability mass shifts between classes. Input A concentrates mass heavily on the first class, whereas Input B distributes its mass more evenly across options.\n\nIn practice, temperature scaling adjusts this sharpness before normalization. A lower temperature amplifies differences, while a higher temperature smooths the probabilities out.",
