  "body": "Predicting the mean target value provides a simple constant baseline for any regression task. This baseline ignores all feature inputs and always guesses the average of the training targets. By minimizing squared error, the optimal constant prediction is precisely the arithmetic mean $\\bar{y}$.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nComparing a model's performance against this constant prediction helps verify if the learned features add any genuine predictive value. If a model fails to beat the mean baseline, it has failed to capture the underlying patterns in the data. The residual sum of squares from this baseline also forms the denominator in the coefficient of determination $R^2$.\n\nIn practice, this baseline establishes the minimum performance threshold that any regression algorithm must exceed. Calculating it requires only summing the target values and dividing by the count of samples $n$. Thus, $\\bar{y} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} y_i$ gives the exact prediction used across all inputs.",
