  "body": "When a language model generates text, it computes raw scores for every vocabulary token and applies the softmax function to turn them into a probability distribution.\n\nTop-k filtering truncates this distribution by keeping only the $k$ highest-scoring tokens and setting all other token probabilities to zero.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nTo ensure the remaining probabilities still sum to one, the model performs renormalization, dividing each surviving token's original probability by the sum of all kept probabilities.\n\nThis division uniformly scales up the reported probability of every chosen token, meaning the final logged value differs from the initial softmax output.",
