"body": "A confusion matrix tabulates how many instances fall into each true‑vs‑predicted category. The rows show the actual class, the columns the predicted class.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nIn this example the top‑left cell (36) is true negatives, the top‑right (8) false positives, the bottom‑left (45) false negatives, and the bottom‑right (60) true positives. From these numbers we compute precision $\\frac{TP}{TP+FP}=\\frac{60}{68}=0.88$ and recall $\\frac{TP}{TP+FN}=\\frac{60}{105}=0.57$.\n\nPrecision tells how many predicted positives are correct, while recall tells how many actual positives were captured. Both metrics together reveal the trade‑off between missing positives and flagging negatives incorrectly.",
